{"name":"Rufous","hex":"#a81c07","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rufous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish colour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of rufous hummingbird.","A reddish-brown colour, as of rust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rufous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rufous","blocks":[{"text":"Rufous is a colour that may be described as reddish-brown or brownish-red, as of rust or oxidised iron. The first recorded use of rufous as a colour name in English was in 1782. However, the colour is also recorded earlier in 1527 as a diagnostic urine colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Rufous-necked_hornbill_1.jpg/330px-Rufous-necked_hornbill_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rufous","wikidata":"Q7377969"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg/500px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg/1280px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg/500px-Luscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Common nightingale a.k.a. \"rufous nightingale\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALuscinia_megarhynchos_-_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Rufous_Horseshoe_Bat_%28Rhinolophus_rouxii%29_%286747960629%29.jpg/500px-Rufous_Horseshoe_Bat_%28Rhinolophus_rouxii%29_%286747960629%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/